                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b4a2a007-55c0-4dab-b9c0-851954484817",
                                "sense_id": "19c3b58c-bc43-3733-921b-1246dc7984d8",
                                "text": "Birds' dung has been held in high regard since time immemorial as a fertiliser, and the fact that this wonderful new manure was composed of birds' dung, and had a strong manurial smell, undoubtedly helped it to come rapidly into favour among farmers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6e0435c0-a69e-4fd5-9c6f-84d5fe8c005d",
                                "sense_id": "19c3b58c-bc43-3733-921b-1246dc7984d8",
                                "text": "1894, Ivan Dexter, Talmud: A Strange Narrative of Central Australia, published in serial form in Port Adelaide News and Lefevre's Peninsula Advertiser (SA), Chapter XXVI, http://gutenberg.net.au/ebooks16/1600641.txt\nI understood from Anscra that all the filth and refuse of the settlement—except a certain portion kept for manurial purposes, and sent to the plantation—was thrown into this torrent nightly and swept perhaps hundreds of miles away."
                            }
                        ]
